---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const APP_URL = "https://app.tarnhome.com";
---

<Layout
  title="How Tarn Works"
  description="Tarn pulls permit history, code-era timelines, and public records into one report — the fourth opinion alongside your walkthrough, your agent, and your inspector."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1>Public records, read the way a buyer needs them read.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The information already exists — permit filings, code adoption dates, municipal
        records. It's just scattered, technical, and not written for you. Tarn pulls it
        together and translates it into what it means for the house you're looking at.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps">
    <div class="wrap steps-grid">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <h2>Enter an address</h2>
        <p>Tarn checks it against permit records for that city — building, electrical, plumbing, mechanical, and fire, where available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <h2>See what's on record</h2>
        <p>Every permit found, with dates and type — a factual history of work that was done and inspected, not just claimed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <h2>See what the code era implies</h2>
        <p>Systems installed before a given code adoption date get flagged as considerations, not alarms — knob-and-tube wiring, galvanized plumbing, and similar code-era risks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">4</span>
        <h2>Tell us what's missing</h2>
        <p>Tarn is new and free while it's being built. Every report ends with a question: what wasn't useful here? That's what shapes what we build next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-cta">
    <div class="wrap page-cta-inner">
      <h2>Try it on a real address</h2>
      <a href={APP_URL} class="btn btn-primary">Search an address</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    background: var(--charter-navy);
    color: var(--cream);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    color: var(--cream);
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
  }
  .lead {
    max-width: 620px;
    opacity: 0.9;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .steps {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }
  .steps-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .step {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .step-num {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    line-height: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--glacial-teal);
    color: var(--white);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .step h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .step p {
    color: var(--slate);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .steps-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .page-cta {
    background: var(--white);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 3rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .page-cta-inner h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
